@* NFR-24: the one icon set. The design system's 31 line glyphs, drawn on a 24px grid and rendered
   inline, so an action's glyph costs no webfont, no sprite request and no third stylesheet link -
   App.razor is pinned to exactly two.

   The paint is declared once, on the wrapper: `fill="none"` and `stroke="currentColor"`, which is
   the only colour keyword NFR-29's scanner allows. Every glyph is therefore an outline in the
   colour of the text it sits beside, and follows a token wherever it is placed - including onto the
   dark navigation. `stroke-width` and the round caps live here too rather than on each path, so
   thirty-one glyphs cannot drift into thirty-one weights.

   Path data is transcribed from `design-system/assets/Icons/icons.json`. Independent @if blocks
   rather than a switch expression in markup: an `else` reads to NFR-14's scan as a rendered English
   word, and the conditions are mutually exclusive anyway. *@

<svg class="dt-icon"
     viewBox="0 0 24 24"
     fill="none"
     stroke="currentColor"
     stroke-width="2"
     stroke-linecap="round"
     stroke-linejoin="round"
     aria-hidden="true"
     focusable="false"
     xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    @if (Name == IconName.Home)
    {
        <path d="M3 11l9-8 9 8M5 10v10h14V10M10 20v-6h4v6" />
    }
    @if (Name == IconName.Profile)
    {
        <circle cx="12" cy="8" r="4" />
        <path d="M4 21c0-4 4-6 8-6s8 2 8 6" />
    }
    @if (Name == IconName.SignIn)
